@lucaspar btw my workaround for this

`.zshrc`
```
unalias ls 2>/dev/null
function ls {
	eza -g --header --classify --icons=auto --color=auto --group-directories-first "${@:-.}"
}
```

@yugdabgar21  I built something along these lines, a desktop pet [https://github.com/g3saranath/opencode-pet](https://github.com/g3saranath/opencode-pet) (currently a Harry Potter on a broom, easily reskinned) that sits on top of your screen and reflects your opencode session live: idle/thinking/working/sleeping states, a live status bubble showing the current tool/action, and streaming reasoning + tool output in an activity log. It auto-wakes when opencode connects and naps when it disconnects.

It's implemented as an opencode plugin + a separate Electron overlay talking through a small state file (no ports, nothing to configure). Currently tested on macOS but built on standard Electron APIs so Linux/Windows should mostly just work.

Might be a useful reference/starting point for a built-in "Pets" feature - happy to help if there's interest in something like this shipping in core, or in making it easier to swap in custom art per the "Import Pet" idea above.
